# heightfield_visualize

- Label: HeightField Visualize
- Category: Copernicus (`Cop`), Houdini 22.0.368
- Inputs: 1 to 4
- Parameters: 34 (exact, read from Houdini by hython)
- Used by the height graph: no

## Feature summary (web, SideFX reference)

- Source: https://www.sidefx.com/docs/houdini/nodes/cop/heightfield_visualize.html
- Summary (EN): Turns COP layers into geometry and produces a colored heightfield visualization that works like terrain; also converts heightfield layers into geometry usable with SOP heightfield tools.
- Résumé (FR) : Convertit les couches COP en géométrie et produit une visualisation colorée de champ de hauteur, utilisable avec les outils heightfield de SOP.

- Inputs meaning: ["height: the layer used as the heightfield", "color: optional layer tinting the surface", "mask: optional layer tinting the surface", "layers: optional cable of extra layers to convert"]

- Key parameters: [{"name": "Height Scale", "meaning": "scales height values into world space, which visualization requires"}, {"name": "Height Offset", "meaning": "shifts the height values"}, {"name": "Split Channels", "meaning": "splits vector volumes into separate float volumes"}, {"name": "Tint by", "meaning": "chooses which layer (Height, Color or Mask) tints the surface"}, {"name": "Input Range / Compute Range", "meaning": "values mapped to the ramp start and end"}, {"name": "Mode", "meaning": "No Ramp, Clamped Ramp or Periodic Ramp, controlling value transform before the ramp"}, {"name": "Diffuse Ramp", "meaning": "color ramp used for the tint"}]

- Caveats: ["Visualization needs world space, so set Height Scale correctly.", "To convert a Mono layer into a heightfield use the Mono to HeightField COP instead."]

